    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "75b34cfdaa66bc6ad256fb02ca069f2b1a87a6b3f479a624055169f7beaded3a",
      "text": "After breakfast, your driver and guide will meet you at the hotel at 08:00. The drive to Yaxhá National Park takes about an hour.\n\nThe park is also known as Guatemala’s Cultural Triangle. Tropical forest surrounds the ruins of ancient cities. The Maya lived here from the second century BC. Temples, palaces, plazas and dwellings survive in the park, where excavations have also uncovered everyday objects.\n\nYaxhá is home to many birds, including the quetzal, a bird held sacred by Indigenous peoples. As you walk through the tropical forest, you may hear howler monkeys.\n\nThe tour ends at the top of Temple 216, the tallest building at the site. You can spend the evening here listening to the birds.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to the San Ignacio area.\n\nOvernight in San Ignacio at Midas Resort.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9larkh-8ge0qr1dl",
        "model": "GPT-6.1-sol"
